// Sleepstick

@0 = ~Sleepstick~
@1 = ~Sleepstick~

@10 = ~The Sleepstick is a blackjack–a light weapon that consists of a small leather bag filled with a heavyweight material, attached to a flexible wooden stick. With its small size, it can be easily concealed, and is therefore favored by less reputable characters.

Because of the small size the weapon can deal only minor non-lethal damage. However, unsuspecting targets can be knocked unconscious by administering a well-aimed blow to the head or back of the neck.

STATISTICS:

Combat abilities:
– When a backstab is performed the victim is knocked unconscious for 1d4+2 rounds if the wielder is proficient in handling the weapon. A successful save vs. Death with a penalty that increases with the amount of points spent in the weapon proficiency negates the effect. Undead, myconids, and constructs are immune to the effect.
– The victim is rendered unconscious if a hit from the weapon reduces their hit points to 0.

Damage: 1d2 (non-lethal)
Speed Factor: 2
Proficiency Type: Club
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 3 Strength

Weight: 1~
@11 = ~The Sleepstick is a blackjack–a light weapon that consists of a small leather bag filled with a heavyweight material, attached to a flexible wooden stick. With its small size, it can be easily concealed, and is therefore favored by less reputable characters.

